From 740dab892f556f9bc793622150873848f1e7c751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:29:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 85/85] ntdll: Run the Rockstar Games Launcher on Mullion with
 WFDXCompat's companion, as on arm64.

The Rockstar Games Launcher and SocialClubHelper ran on D3DMetal with WFDXCompat's launcher
companion, where their UI's D3D11 device could not be created on any route, so the launcher
quit with "failed to initialize" (metalsharp/MetalSharp-Wine#113). The arm64 runtime runs them
on Mullion with the companion only interposing device creation, which works. This does the same:
- graphics_policy.c: a launcher process the policy selects runs on Mullion when its runtime is
  there, with the companion when that is there too, whatever GRAPHICS_BACKEND says.
- wfdxcompat_loader.c (unix): the companion needs Mullion, not D3DMetal, and is found by name only
  in the processes the policy selected, as on arm64.
- wfdxcompat_loader.c: those processes give the companion INTERPOSE | NATIVE_D3D10 (0x11), as on
  arm64: Mullion implements D3D10, context state and GDI surfaces itself.
  WFDXCOMPAT_LAUNCHER_FLAGS overrides. The flags have names; Epic's self-update service keeps
  INTERPOSE | SERVICE_SWAPCHAIN on D3DMetal.

The companion must be WFDXCompat's with NATIVE_D3D10 at 0x10 (source/wfdxcompat). WFDXCompat's
runtime directory is found next to Wine when WFDXCOMPAT_RUNTIME_DIR isn't set, as before, so this
works in any prefix without per-game settings.
